{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And if it be eaten, etc.</b> If it does not concern outside its time — for it was already stated ״וְאִם הֵאָכֹל יֵאָכֵל מִבְּשַׂר זֶבַח שְׁלָמָיו וְגוֹ׳״ (Leviticus 7) — apply it to outside its place. One might say they are liable to excision for eating it — therefore Scripture says ״וְהַנֶּפֶשׁ הָאֹכֶלֶת מִמֶּנּוּ עֲוֹנָהּ תִּשָּׂא״ — ״מִמֶּנּוּ״ and not its fellow; this excludes the one slaughtered with intent outside its place (Zevaḥim 28)." "<b>An abomination.</b> Detestable, as in ״וּמְרַק פִּגֻּלִים כֻּלֵּיהֶם״ (Isaiah 65)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:05.315215696Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}